  // Bodies fit their world. A coat is rolled from what the climate lists; banned bodies can't
  // live there at all. bulk is girth, limbs is legs, necks and tails, ears are for shedding heat,
  // pale and tan are how far a coat goes to snow or sand.
  // What each world's story leaves walking it: its own kinds, each made from the bestiary's parts (one of the
  // world's people, machines or beasts, and what is done to them), weighted by its fall (or, failing a line of its
  // own, the fall's group), its theme and the rest of its roll (creed.x, presence.y); the most it has; how many
  // groups of them are kept within reach of you; what everyone on the world wears for its story ("folk", by fall
  // group, fall and theme, added together); and what each era (the living's tech: Low, Mid, High) arms, dresses and
  // swaps on people. Kinds: body person|machine|beast; occupancy Friendly|Raider|Feral; roles their bodies were;
  // mutation and wrongs (jaw, arm, hunch, head) as ranges; skin pulled toward a colour; cloth "" (their own),
  // "uniform" (one colour from the world's paint), "festive" (bright, faded) or "list" (colours); strip slots or
  // garments (and "prop"); look as a job's look; armed (the era's arms); behaviour, temper, hunts, flees; walk, run
  // and health as multipliers; group; haunts town|ruins|road|open by weight; night (more by night); den (they
  // hold twisted beasts' places too).
